WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:07.799
I'll use my forklift to lift it out
so we can get it to the barn.

00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:10.260
What do you think,&nbsp; Sal?

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.179
I think...I think...

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.223
I think you're the heartiest
helper who has ever

00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:17.058
helped anyone with their heart.

00:00:17.058 --> 00:00:19.436
Thank you! Thank you! Thank you!

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:24.107
I am Loren Long and I'm
an author and illustrator

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:26.359
for children's picture books.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.986
Hi, I'm Otis.

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:30.405
Otis is a friendly little tractor.

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:33.742
He has a big heart.

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:34.451
We can do this together.

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:38.538
Sometimes he can do it on his own.
Sometimes it takes teamwork.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.581
I can help you.

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:41.041
We'll help too.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.627
He's a tractor who works
hard and plays hard.

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:45.837
And that's a beautiful thing.

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:47.005
Woohoo!

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:53.970
I wrote the first self-titled book
just as a one-off story.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:57.724
I had no idea that it was something
that would really resonate

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.850
and find an audience.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.061
Oooooh!

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.563
On Get Rolling with Otis,

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:08.610
they actually created a piece of Otis'
motor that's in the shape of a heart.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.072
An you wouldn't really
notice it until Otis feels.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:17.410
And so children will see Otis
recognize something, and feel it.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.037
Can I help?

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:21.289
And then compassion comes in,

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:22.665
compassionate action.

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:23.583
Got it!

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:27.253
Otis is not just an observer,
but he's also a doer.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.506
Let's get rolling!

00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:33.093
The theme through all of
Get Rolling with Otis

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:39.015
is the unselfishness and the ability
for Otis to feel what it's like

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:42.185
to be one of the animals and
to care for his friends.

00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:43.103
Baaa?

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.687
Baaa!

00:01:44.687 --> 00:01:49.400
The ability to walk in someone else's
shoes is such a great strength and

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.613
if we can model empathy
and teach empathy to children,

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:58.701
then I think we can
change the world a little bit.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.703
Empathy is a superpower.

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:04.666
Otis teaches young children that
they can make a difference.

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:08.169
If they just take a moment to
notice somebody else's feelings,

00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:11.381
that they can put on their
own brakes, stop and go,

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:13.424
"Oooh. How would I feel
if that happened to me?"

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:15.552
Can you help me?

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:17.178
I could try.

00:02:17.178 --> 00:02:19.931
Otis can be the model
that helps our kids learn that

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:23.810
empathy is doable and
empathy is strong and powerful.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.395
Thanks, Otis.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:28.690
We're so happy to
have friends like you.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:32.277
I was trying to model the behavior
of goodness and kindness

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:34.237
and caring for others.

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:39.492
To have a part in this television
project, I wanted to make sure

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.245
the heart of Otis was in that show.

00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:45.165
On our farm, we all help each other.

